/* WEEKS = the 18 weeks of the semester, one row per week for BOTH courses (= the week table of the ED2 assessment plan):
   teaching weeks 1–8, written midterm week 9 (MCP practical midterm in its afternoon), teaching weeks 10–16, review and make-ups week 17
   (MCP practical final in its afternoon), written final week 18 (no MCP session). MCP week numbers ARE these semester week numbers.
   Row: wk; kind 'teach' | 'exam' | 'review'; ed2 = the MORNING:
     ch (chapter), part (1 | 2 when a chapter takes two weeks), title / en (what the morning is about),
     pages = the ED2 page files of the morning in reading order — FILLED IN BELOW from STOPS[].wk (write the week on the stop, not here),
     label / label_en = chapter and part in words ("chapter 5, part 1"; the title for exam and review weeks) and
     range / range_en = the same with the pages ("chapter 5, part 1 (pages 5.1–5.5)") — both filled in below,
     pre = chapter of the pre-test at the start of the morning ('' = none; diag: true = diagnostic only, not scored),
     lab = lab sheet id ('1' … '5A', '5B' …; handed out on paper), labPage = the ED2 page that explains that lab sheet (its section #tL),
     sim = chapter of the end-of-chapter simulation task at the end of the morning ('' = none); its circuit drawn by hand on the A4 sheet
       is the homework ED2-HW<sim>, handed in at the start of the next session,
     soon: true = chapter not built yet, event 'midterm' | 'review' | 'final' (exam and review weeks), note / note_en = one remark;
   mcp = the AFTERNOON = the MCP_WEEKS entry of the same week (linked below; null in week 18). EN strings hold no Thai. */
